---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Web apps — LemmaScript Solutions"
  description="Agents can build a web app end to end. LemmaScript makes the load-bearing logic — money, inventory, access, counts — correct by construction, so you can hand your agent the build and trust what ships."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="kicker">// solutions / web apps</span>
      <h1>Let your agent build the app. <em>Guarantee the logic that can't be wrong.</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Agents can write a web app end to end now — routes, views, data access. What keeps you
        reading every line is the logic where a wrong answer is a disaster: money, inventory,
        access, counts. LemmaScript lets the agent make that logic correct by construction — so
        you can hand over the build and trust what ships.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- WHERE AUTONOMY IS SAFE — the stack -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head center" style="margin-inline:auto">
        <span class="kicker">// where autonomy is safe</span>
        <h2>Most of a web app is glue. A little of it is load-bearing.</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">
          An agent can write the UI, the routes, the data access — and a slip there is a quick fix.
          The load-bearing logic is different: allocation, balances, permissions, counts, where one
          wrong answer means overselling, a double charge, a hole in your access control. Pin a
          contract to that logic and the agent iterates until it's correct by construction.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="stack">
        <div class="stack-bar"><span class="stack-name">booking-app</span><span class="stack-hint">one codebase, mostly agent-written</span></div>
        <div class="stack-body">
          <div class="layer"><span>UI · forms · views</span><span class="layer-tag">agent-written</span></div>
          <div class="layer"><span>routes · request handlers</span><span class="layer-tag">agent-written</span></div>
          <div class="layer"><span>services · glue</span><span class="layer-tag">agent-written</span></div>

          <div class="layer-core">
            <div class="core-head">
              <span class="core-name">core · allocate()</span>
              <span class="badge badge-verified"><span class="bdot"></span>Guaranteed</span>
            </div>
            <code class="core-contract">//@ ensures sum(\result) === total</code>
            <span class="core-note">never oversells · correct for every input, by construction</span>
          </div>

          <div class="layer"><span>database · I/O</span><span class="layer-tag">agent-written</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="stack-legend">The agent builds the whole stack. One layer carries a contract — and that layer can't be wrong.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE GUARANTEE, IN CODE -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="kicker">// the guarantee, in code</span>
        <h2>You review one line of intent. The agent writes the rest.</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">
          The agent pins a contract to the function that carries the invariant, then iterates
          until the code satisfies it for every input. What surfaces is correct code — and all
          you have to read is the guarantee on top.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="code-compare">
        <div class="codeblock">
          <div class="code-bar">
            <span class="code-file">src/domain.ts</span>
            <span class="code-label">the agent's first pass</span>
          </div>
          <pre class="code-body"><span class="t-cmt">// counting logic — no guarantee on what it returns</span>
<span class="t-kw">export function</span> <span class="t-fn">hasRoom</span>(p: Page, idx: number): boolean &#123;
  <span class="t-kw">return</span> confirmedCount(p.bookings, idx) &lt; capacityAt(p.slots, idx)
&#125;</pre>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
        <div class="codeblock compare-after">
          <div class="code-bar">
            <span class="code-file">src/domain.ts</span>
            <span class="badge badge-verified" style="margin-left:auto">Guaranteed</span>
          </div>
          <pre class="code-body"><span class="t-cmt">//</span><span class="t-at">@</span> <span class="t-dir-contract">contract</span> <span class="t-prose">The room only ever reports available when it truly has capacity.</span>
<span class="t-kw">export function</span> <span class="t-fn">hasRoom</span>(p: Page, idx: number): boolean &#123;
  <span class="t-cmt">//</span><span class="t-at">@</span> <span class="t-dir-ensures">ensures</span> <span class="t-annokw"><span class="t-result">\result</span> === (</span>
  <span class="t-cmt">//   0 &lt;= idx &amp;&amp; idx &lt; p.slots.length &amp;&amp;</span>
  <span class="t-cmt">//   confirmedCount(p.bookings, idx) &lt; capacityAt(p.slots, idx)</span>
  <span class="t-cmt">// )</span>
  <span class="t-kw">if</span> (idx &lt; <span class="t-num">0</span>) <span class="t-kw">return</span> <span class="t-kw">false</span>
  <span class="t-kw">if</span> (idx &gt;= p.slots.length) <span class="t-kw">return</span> <span class="t-kw">false</span>
  <span class="t-kw">return</span> confirmedCount(p.bookings, idx) &lt; capacityAt(p.slots, idx)
&#125;</pre>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="code-caption">
        From <a href="https://github.com/midspiral/quota-lemmascript" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-arrow">quota-lemmascript ↗</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT IT UNLOCKS -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="kicker">// what it unlocks</span>
        <h2>Hand over the build. Keep the guarantees.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="what-grid">
        <div class="what-item">
          <h3>Ship without reading every line</h3>
          <p>You review the contract — the one line that says what the code must do — not the implementation the agent wrote underneath it. If it satisfies the contract, it's correct.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="what-item">
          <h3>Correct under real traffic</h3>
          <p>A contract that holds for every input holds regardless of arrival order — concurrent bookings, retries, races. The invariant can't be broken by timing or load.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="what-item">
          <h3>Safe to let it refactor</h3>
          <p>Turn the agent loose on the core and it can rewrite freely. Any change that breaks the invariant fails the check immediately — not in production weeks later.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- REAL EXAMPLE -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="kicker">// in the wild</span>
        <h2>A booking app that can't overbook — by construction.</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">
          Quota lets providers publish a limited number of slots and users claim them. The agent
          built the app; its core allocation logic carries a contract that guarantees it never
          oversells — no matter how many people book at once, or in what order.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="ex-stats">
        <div class="ex-stat">
          <span class="ex-val">0</span>
          <span class="ex-label">chance of overselling a slot</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ex-stat">
          <span class="ex-val">1</span>
          <span class="ex-label">contract on the logic that matters</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ex-stat">
          <span class="ex-val">rest</span>
          <span class="ex-label">of the app, agent-built</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ex-actions">
        <a href="/case-studies/quota" class="btn btn-primary">Read the case study →</a>
        <a href="/solutions" class="btn btn-secondary">All solutions</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* ---------- the app stack: agent-built layers, one guaranteed core ---------- */
  .stack {
    max-width: 600px;
    margin: var(--sp-10) auto 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--r-xl);
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .stack-bar {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--sp-3);
    padding: var(--sp-3) var(--sp-4);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-caption);
  }
  .stack-name { color: var(--text-secondary); font-weight: 600; }
  .stack-hint { color: var(--text-faint); }
  .stack-body { padding: var(--sp-4); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--sp-2); }

  .layer {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--sp-3);
    padding: var(--sp-3) var(--sp-4);
    border-radius: var(--r-md);
    background: var(--bg-inset);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-caption);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .layer-tag { color: var(--text-faint); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; font-size: 0.68rem; }

  .layer-core {
    padding: var(--sp-5);
    border-radius: var(--r-md);
    background: var(--state-verified-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--accent-dim);
    box-shadow: var(--elev-glow);
  }
  .core-head { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--sp-3); margin-bottom: var(--sp-3); }
  .core-name { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--fs-small); font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); }
  .core-contract { display: block; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--fs-small); color: var(--accent); }
  .core-note { display: block; margin-top: var(--sp-2); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--fs-caption); color: var(--text-secondary); }

  .stack-legend {
    max-width: 600px;
    margin: var(--sp-4) auto 0;
    text-align: center;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-caption);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  /* ---------- before/after code compare ---------- */
  .code-compare {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr;
    gap: var(--sp-4);
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-4);
  }
  .compare-arrow {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    text-align: center;
    padding: 0 var(--sp-2);
  }
  .compare-after { box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--accent-dim), var(--elev-glow); }
  .code-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-caption);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-left: auto;
  }
  .code-caption {
    font-size: var(--fs-caption);
    color: var(--text-faint);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  /* ---------- shared grids ---------- */
  .what-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: var(--sp-4); }
  .what-item { background: var(--bg-surface); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--r-lg); padding: var(--sp-6); }
  .what-item h3 { font-size: var(--fs-h3); margin-bottom: var(--sp-3); }
  .what-item p { font-size: var(--fs-small); color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.65; }

  .ex-stats { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: var(--sp-4); margin-bottom: var(--sp-10); }
  .ex-stat { background: var(--bg-surface); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--r-lg); padding: var(--sp-6); }
  .ex-val { display: block; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: var(--sp-2); }
  .ex-label { font-size: var(--fs-small); color: var(--text-muted); }
  .ex-actions { display: flex; gap: var(--sp-3); flex-wrap: wrap; }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .code-compare { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .compare-arrow { transform: rotate(90deg); }
    .what-grid, .ex-stats { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
